  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 7901.04 Determination of Missing Adult",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 7901.04 Determination of Missing Adult.\n\n(a) Upon receiving notice of a missing person, a local law enforcement agency shall determine if the person is a missing adult as defined in RSA 106-J:1.\n\n(b) In making such a determination, if the local law enforcement agency is notified that the person has a cognitive or mental disability, or other related disability, the law enforcement agency may determine whether the person is considered a missing vulnerable adult as defined in RSA 106-J:3, III.\n\n(c) If the local law enforcement agency determines a person to be a missing adult, the agency shall initiate the reporting procedure set forth in this part Saf-C 7901.\n\n(d) If the local law enforcement agency determines a person to be a missing vulnerable adult, the agency shall initiate the alert activation procedures set forth in part Saf-C 7902.\n\nSource. #14199, eff 2-25-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c7900.html"
